# Environment contract.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here is read by the
# build today unless the comment says otherwise — this file exists so the
# missing pieces are visible rather than discovered mid-slice.
#
# There is no server in this repository. That is the single most important
# thing to know about this file: the client has no backend to point at yet.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by code today
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# apps/mobile — the tenant engine origin the WebView loads. Inlined into the
# Expo bundle at build time, so changing it requires a rebuild, not a restart.
# Defaults to http://localhost:4174 when unset.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENGINE_ORIGIN=http://localhost:4174

# tooling/telemetry/verify-queue.mjs — set to 1 to reuse an already compiled
# copy of apps/web/src/telemetry.ts instead of recompiling it. Only useful when
# iterating on the harness itself.
# SOP_SKIP_COMPILE=1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reserved for the transport slice. NOT read by any code yet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The next slice adds authenticated bundle delivery and telemetry ingest. These
# are the variables it will need, named now so the shape is reviewable before
# anything depends on it. Do not add code that reads them until the transport
# exists — a variable that is set but unread is a false signal that the feature
# is configured.
#
# The project ref and URL are public (they appear in every API request) and are
# filled in. The anon key and the database password are secrets and are not.

# Supabase project: lxlokqtowvaesxjishqz
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://lxlokqtowvaesxjishqz.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Supabase CLI and migration tooling. Server-side only — never expose these to
# the browser bundle or commit them. The CLI stores its own copy after
# `supabase login`; these exist for CI, where there is no keyring.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=lxlokqtowvaesxjishqz
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=
